  "result": "Done. The `ratelimit` package is implemented and the full suite passes.\n\n```\n5 passed in 0.03s\n```\n\n**What I did**\n- Wrote `ratelimit/limiter.py` with the `RateLimiter` class from the spec. The package `__init__.py` was already present and untouched.\n- Constructor validates that the limit is a positive integer and the window is positive.\n- Spot-checked fractional refill boundaries and a backwards-moving clock beyond what the tests cover. Both behave sensibly: a clock that goes backwards is treated as zero elapsed time rather than draining tokens.\n- Nothing is committed. The new file and pytest caches are untracked in the working tree, since you did not ask for a commit.\n\n**Approach chosen:** Approach A, the token bucket. It needs only two numbers per key, so memory is O(1) regardless of the limit, and refill is computed as elapsed times limit divided by window so that exact multiples of the window restore whole tokens without floating-point drift breaking the boundary cases.",
